Create Japan’s classic “henohenomoheji” face art on your phone.
Swap the characters for the brows, eyes, nose, mouth, and outline to make your own face.

Beyond hiragana and katakana, you can pick parts from many scripts — Latin letters, Hangul, Thai, Myanmar, Hindi, Kannada, Georgian, Tibetan, and more.

【Features】
・Choose parts from kana charts and other writing-system charts
・Multilingual characters including Thai, Hangul, and Latin
・Support for dakuten, handakuten, and small kana
・Keyboard input
・Scale, move, and rotate each part
・Linked transforms for brows and for eyes
・Color changes
・Save faces to an album and edit them later
・Save and share as an image (LINE, X, and more)
・Export / import album data
・Japanese / English UI

Fun for kids and adults — a quick break, or a catchy image for a message.
How would you write henohenomoheji?
